{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "העטופים", :translit "ha'atufim", :gloss "the wrapped/enveloped ones"} {:he "העטופים ללבן", :translit "ha'atufim la-lavan", :gloss "the wrapped ones for Laban"} {:he "העטופים ברעב", :translit "ha'atufim ba-ra'av", :gloss "enveloped in famine"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["העטופים ללבן" "העטופים ברעב"]}], :frame {:text "In Genesis 30:42, Jacob separates the strong animals for himself and gives the lean ones ('העטופים') to Laban. The Ba'al HaTurim reads this moment on two levels: practically, the lean animals perish from hunger; and teleologically, Jacob's act of appearing to use trickery ('רמאות') generates consequences for his own descendants, who are later enveloped in famine — the same root רעב connects the lean animals' fate to the famine that drives Jacob's sons down to Egypt in Genesis 41–42, where Joseph's brothers must seek sustenance.", :sources ["Genesis 30:42" "Genesis 41:54-57" "Genesis 42:1-3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["העטופים ללבן" "העטופים ברעב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "העטופים ללבן", :refs ["Genesis 30:42"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "העטופים ברעב", :refs ["Lamentations 2:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:19.120007618Z", :model "glm-5.2"}